# Reviewed exceptions for the image scan (.github/workflows/image-scan.yml).
# Policy and review rules: docs/ci/image-scanning.md
#
# One finding ID per line. Every entry needs, in the comment lines directly
# above it, a Reason: and an Owner:, and an exp:YYYY-MM-DD on the ID line
# itself (at most 90 days ahead). Trivy stops ignoring an entry after its
# expiry date, so the finding comes back until someone re-reviews it.
#
# Example (do not uncomment, the ID is made up):
#   # Reason: vendor confirmed the code path is not reachable in this image
#   # Owner: @github-handle  Ref: https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>
#   CVE-2099-00000 exp:2099-01-31
